  "title": "Accessmedicine Klinisches Wissen Aktuell Und Online",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Access knowledge",
      "text": "- external pageHarrison’s Principles of Internal Medicinecall\\_made\n\n- external pageGoodman &amp; Gilman’s:call\\_madeexternal pageThe Pharmacological Basis of Therapeuticscall\\_made\n\n- external pageCURRENT Medical Diagnosis &amp; Treatmentcall\\_made\n\n- external pageTintinalli’s Emergency Medicinecall\\_made\n\n- Diagnosaurus: More than 1,000 differential diagnoses that can be searched by symptom, illness or organ system\n\n- Quick Medical Diagnosis &amp; Treatment (external pageQMDTcall\\_made): Quick orientation in terms of clinical findings and treatment options for known illnesses\n\nAs a member of the ETH Zurich community, you now have access to the AccessMedicine database as well as the AccessEmergency Medicine sub-database. This means that a relevant and comprehensive online source of medical knowledge is available to you so that you can expand your knowledge, substantiate your hypotheses and advance your research."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Access knowledge",
      "text": "In both learning environments, you have access to the latest editions of more than 100 textbooks and medical references, including the following works:"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Visualise knowledge",
      "text": "The databases also include case studies, procedural videos and animations that help support visual diagnosis.\n\nAt the same time, the QuickReference tools allow for quick, targeted searches and provide you with current, comprehensive information."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Test your knowledge",
      "text": "After registering for free, you can test your acquired knowledge and prepare yourself optimally for exams: answer the online practice questions and solve test problems."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Staffnet",
      "text": "#KnowMore – The prepared content issued by the ETH Library is at your free disposal and gives you a head start.\n\n#ETHLibraryDigital – The ETH Library is there for you digitally with various resources and services , not only during the COVID-19 protective measures."
    }
  ],
